{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam documentation and portability","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG",".bridge_state/projects.json","status","type","link","priority","create_defaults"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","mapping seam","provider-neutral","migration safety","backward compatibility","configuration"],"propositions":["The mapping seam requires comprehensive end-to-end documentation covering config surface, echo-safe behaviors, and probe command across docs/config.md, docs/mapping-seam.md, and docs/README.md.","The mapping seam must be provider-neutral with no capability whose only trigger is a specific CI provider; the feature must work across diverse or absent CI environments.","The feature is additive and backward-compatible: an absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section reproduces current hardcoded behavior exactly, and rollback is achieved by deleting the section.","Portability is substantiated by injected-transport unit tests in S1-S8 that require no live Jira and no specific CI provider; the probe degrades to offline emit and is never a CI gate."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787545378044327001,"uuid":"d9816f27-3b4a-4b74-89b6-5c84d03ced91"}